   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to expanding the waiver\nof the residency requirement for the city attorney in the city of\nMechanicville, Saratoga county",
    "basePrintNo": "S2288",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2288-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2288\n\nSPONSOR: JORDAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to expanding the\nwaiver of the residency requirement for the city attorney in the city of\nMechanicville, Saratoga county\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 expands the residency requirement exception for city attorney\nof Mechanicville to counties adjoining Saratoga County.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill is a correction to Chapter 461 of the Laws of 2019. It expands\nthe previous residency requirement exception that Chapter 461 to include\nall counties adjoining Saratoga County.  This legislation comes at the\nrequest of the City of Mechanicville.  The vacancy in the Office of City\nAttorney, which began on December 318t, 2018, has come with a difficulty\nin finding qualified candidates to fill the role. The City of Mechanic-\nville has requested authorization to look beyond the City's boundaries.\nThis bill would allow them to search for qualified candidates among\nresidents of Saratoga County or any adjoining county.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nS7006 (2020) - Referred to Investigations and Government Operations\n\nS2068 (2019) - Signed as Chapter 461 of the Laws of 2019.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
